# MS-COCO, test samples = the class object LangSAM detects in each of the 500 test images: its box (+10 %
# context), cut in memory (crop references, JSON only; preprocessing/build_detected_test_set.py
# --test-dir data/coco_common10/val --out data/coco_common10/detected_test). A full COCO image shows
# several of the 10 classes but is scored against one; a box around the detected object is one object.
# 495 of 500 images have a detection (handbag 45); median IoU with the COCO box 0.96. Grids: 2x2 of the
# crops. Source after coco.env; the concepts (steps 1-5) are the coco runs' (run_experiments.py tgcl).
IMAGE_ROOT_SINGLE=data/coco_common10/detected_test/test.json
IMAGE_ROOT_GRID=data/coco_common10/detected_test/grids.json
IMAGE_ROOT=${IMAGE_ROOT_SINGLE}
